# ==== T-FMT-B — SYNONYM: the `_`-CONTINUATION BOUNDARY shapes for `await`.
# PIN (Core #12 escape hatch — this cell has no breakable mechanism under the
# typed design, so it states what it pins instead): identifiers may begin with
# the letters of a keyword (`[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*`), so `await_x` is an
# ORDINARY function name, not the `await` keyword plus `_x`. A source-SCAN
# oracle ("does the text at this span start with `await`?") reports a false
# positive here; the typed `prefix_form` flag written by the parser cannot.
# This fixture is the standing evidence that the scan-based design was
# rejected for cause: it must format to itself under the typed design, and a
# future contributor who "simplifies" the flag back into a span sniff will see
# `await_x().await()` rewritten to `await await_x()` and know why.
async int await_x():
    return 1

async void g():
    int a = await_x().await()
    int b = await await_x()
    print(a + b)

async void main():
    await g()
